From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cloud-comms-engine <engine@diegonmarcos.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] add com.diegonmarcos.comms.chat client to google-services.json

The com.google.gms.google-services Gradle plugin matches google-services.json
against the applicationId (not the namespace as patch 0001 assumed), so the
repackaged applicationId com.diegonmarcos.comms.chat had "No matching client
found" and failed :app:processReleaseGoogleServices. Add a client entry cloned
from the com.mattermost.rnbeta beta client (same upstream Firebase project).
Push remains effectively disabled for this self-compiled fork (delivery is tied
to the upstream project's sender), but Firebase resource generation + init now
succeed so the release build completes.
diff --git a/android/app/google-services.json b/android/app/google-services.json
index 6b71b966d..96d5ddc39 100644
--- a/android/app/google-services.json
+++ b/android/app/google-services.json
@@ -77,6 +77,35 @@
           ]
         }
       }
+    },
+    {
+      "client_info": {
+        "mobilesdk_app_id": "1:184930218130:android:c7debfa7ea3f75a7",
+        "android_client_info": {
+          "package_name": "com.diegonmarcos.comms.chat"
+        }
+      },
+      "oauth_client": [
+        {
+          "client_id": "184930218130-8nahrspll1opff0uogtkh2qsv8coqngo.apps.googleusercontent.com",
+          "client_type": 3
+        }
+      ],
+      "api_key": [
+        {
+          "current_key": "AIzaSyASRwdI3DKpyjt_gMbL1MpViI3BTHB9rFg"
+        }
+      ],
+      "services": {
+        "appinvite_service": {
+          "other_platform_oauth_client": [
+            {
+              "client_id": "109751306267633962395",
+              "client_type": 3
+            }
+          ]
+        }
+      }
     }
   ],
   "configuration_version": "1"
